{"skill":{"slug":"agent-browser-3","displayName":"Agent Browser"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769694571134,"changelog":"Initial release of agent-browser: Powerful command-line browser automation.\n\n- Automates website navigation, form filling, testing, screenshots, and data extraction.\n- Extensive command set for browser control, interactive element referencing, state checks, and data capture.\n- Supports semantic locators (find by role, label, text, etc.) for robust automation.\n- Provides tools for video recordings, PDF creation, network interception, tab/window management, storage/cookie handling, and more.\n- Includes options for session isolation, headless/headed mode, and structured JSON output.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12895,"sha256":"9caba4d013daf731c9f78803c9a73178400c04e2c033541939d77d0f5bc9248c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/authentication.md","size":4443,"sha256":"5b074030cecb89772b5186f1149285331aa16f1e43b696529413ee1f329427ac","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/proxy-support.md","size":4265,"sha256":"cea752731d94c5ff391898f17d6e4274678b842ff34a8fd49f84fadeb4b1be25","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/session-management.md","size":3894,"sha256":"6a6b97531c40d66097d5d8de19deec34b8dca522806f0ff23d9268029032b7ed","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/snapshot-refs.md","size":4108,"sha256":"96d0a4f8d654937407776cc348a709bbef4c7f8bc6d10f4cc3df36158a9a5beb","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"references/video-recording.md","size":3246,"sha256":"0ce2ecfd6e6637b20a03d60c8383afe2557f86ff4240b53212334c47fe27fc46","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"templates/authenticated-session.sh","size":4235,"sha256":"2d519286316e6cb2c8778b0160192d6a31f5c6803873bc9d18954051b1cbf828","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"templates/capture-workflow.sh","size":1967,"sha256":"82f3bf42bd7ccbc90dcb4aa82e0cab9dba5e6966a01b731736a979ad062e2c04","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"templates/form-automation.sh","size":1590,"sha256":"bfa3e3bb895a8c3ad708a7633610b678ad07493701a2c56033dd36695aa67817","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2557,"sha256":"4967f1d5bef4db5fec6d7eb0c74b72058c86a3e4dc2d933588b92be30522d5c8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789023560504,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0b71ed77f77b5081653512888c82835797b245e688ea2bd4cc2ef81714f00982","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0b71ed77f77b5081653512888c82835797b245e688ea2bd4cc2ef81714f00982","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: agent-browser-3\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills bundle is classified as suspicious due to the broad and high-risk capabilities of the `agent-browser` tool, even though no explicit malicious intent is demonstrated in the provided files. Key indicators include the ability to load custom browser executables and extensions (`--executable-path`, `--extension`, `AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH`, `AGENT_BROWSER_EXTENSIONS`), execute arbitrary JavaScript within the browser context (`agent-browser eval`), access local files via the `file://` protocol, and save/load full browser session state (`agent-browser state save/load`), which can contain sensitive authentication tokens. While these features are plausibly needed for browser automation, they present significant attack surface for potential misuse if the agent or user were compromised, despite the documentation's inclusion of security best practices.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160300337},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":84,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":16,"checkedAt":1789023560504},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This is a legitimate browser automation skill, but it gives agents ways to save reusable logged-in browser sessions and capture page data without enough safeguards for those sensitive artifacts.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Networked browser access and local output files are proportionate for this skill, but users should expect it to interact with arbitrary websites and create durable artifacts such as screenshots, PDFs, recordings, text dumps, and authentication state files.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package contains Markdown documentation and executable shell templates, with no observed dependency installation, remote payload retrieval, scheduled task setup, or tool replacement logic.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are user-directed and do not show prompt hijacking or hidden execution, but sensitive workflows are under-scoped: examples record login flows, save extracted page content, upload local files, and embed proxy credentials without consistent inline warnings or confirmation guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill explicitly supports saving and loading browser state containing cookies and storage, including authenticated and post-2FA sessions; the executable template defaults to ./auth-state.json and documentation shows /tmp/auth-state.json without enforcing restrictive permissions, private directories, or symlink checks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is browser automation for testing, form filling, screenshots, and extraction, and the documented agent-browser commands mostly fit that purpose; the capability set is broad because it includes cookies, storage, JavaScript evaluation, uploads, proxies, screenshots, PDFs, recordings, and saved authentication state.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing if you will use it on real accounts or private sites. Treat auth-state JSON files, recordings, screenshots, PDFs, extracted page text, uploaded files, cookies, storage values, and proxy URLs as sensitive. Store saved browser state outside repositories in private directories with owner-only permissions, avoid persisting post-2FA sessions when possible, use test accounts and synthetic data for recordings, and delete or revoke saved sessions after use.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The flagged screenshots, PDFs, recordings, cookies, storage, extraction, uploads, and proxy credentials are browser-automation features rather than hidden behavior, but the artifact does not consistently warn users that these outputs and examples may expose secrets or personal data.\n[T09] unexpected: The underlying state reuse is purpose-aligned, but the insecure storage concern is supported: templates and references save reusable auth state to predictable or repository-local paths without explicit access-control handling.\n[RA2] expected: Session persistence is disclosed and user-invoked through state save/load, not a hidden background persistence mechanism; the remaining concern is that saved sessions are credential-equivalent and insufficiently protected.\n[TM1] expected: The rm examples are narrow cleanup commands for auth-state files, so the scanner's tool-abuse interpretation is downgraded.\n[MP2] expected: The cited 'fill input' quick-start line is a normal browser form-filling command and does not show context stuffing or memory poisoning.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789023560504}}}}}